Two examples in this repository are derived from that project and are
MODIFIED. They are not copies: each was re-expressed in the BrickWright
pseudocode dialect, targets a different part (STC12C5A60S2 rather than
STC89C52), and compiles through a different toolchain. The circuit each
one drives, and the order of operations it performs, come from the
original.

  examples/08-seven-segment/   derived from 02_7_segment
  examples/09-shift-register/  derived from 01_led_74H595

Both files carry the attribution in their own headers as well.

These two examples exist because that corpus was used to measure what the
dialect could not yet express: 02_7_segment needed whole-port I/O and an
indexed lookup table, and 01_led_74H595 needed a shift-register part. The
examples are the evidence that those gaps closed. See
docs/DIALECT-COVERAGE.md.

